# Must stay last: the first matching rule wins, so a splat placed above these
# would swallow every path named above it.
#
# Cloudflare did not fall back to 404.html on its own here — an unmatched path
# returned a 404 with a zero-length body, which is exactly the blank page the
# custom 404 was written to replace. Serving the file explicitly keeps the
# status honest and still gives the visitor somewhere to go.
#
# The destination is /404, not /404.html: Cloudflare normalises the .html form
# with a 307 to the extensionless path, so a rule pointing at the file resolves
# to a redirect rather than to a body.
#
# KNOWN NOT TO WORK as of 21 Sep 2026, and kept because it is the documented
# mechanism and costs nothing if the cause is fixed. What was established:
#   * 404.html is deployed — /404 returns 200 with the right page
#   * _headers applies to the 404 response, so Pages is generating it
#   * the named rules above work, so _redirects is being read
#   * fresh, never-requested paths behave the same, so it is not edge cache
# An unmatched path still returns 404 with a zero-length body. That points at a
# Pages project setting rather than anything in this repository — check the
# build output directory, and whether a Worker route is bound to the custom
# domain ahead of Pages.
/*                /404               404
